<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Size of the resultant of two pushes</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Two learners push a loaded handcart (mkokoteni) across a flat yard. Seen from above, with east and north positive, their pushes are \(\mathbf{F}_1 = {@col(F1)@}\) N and \(\mathbf{F}_2 = {@col(F2)@}\) N.</p><p>(a) Write the resultant force \(\mathbf{F}_1 + \mathbf{F}_2\).</p><div>\(\mathbf{F}_1 + \mathbf{F}_2 =\) [[input:ans1]] N [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the size of the resultant force, exact or to 2 decimal places.</p><div>[[input:ans2]] N [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Add the east parts and add the north parts: \({@col(F1)@} + {@col(F2)@} = {@tR@}\) N.</p><p>(b) \(|\mathbf{R}| = \sqrt{({@R[1]@})^2 + ({@R[2]@})^2} = \sqrt{{@RR@}}\) [[if test="integerp(tm)"]]\(= {@tm@}\) N.[[else]]\(\approx {@md@}\) N.[[/if]]</p><p>The sizes of the two pushes add up to \({@dispdp(float(g1),2)@}\) N, more than \(|\mathbf{R}|\): the learners push in different directions, so part of each push is wasted.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
col(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]]);
/* Design: size of the resultant of two pushes. The pushes are at a clear angle on every entry (|F1| + |F2| and |F1 - F2| each at least 10 N from |R|). Source: original. */
flist: [[[70,-30],[-30,60]],[[60,-60],[60,10]],[[70,-20],[-10,-60]],[[80,60],[10,60]],[[60,60],[-30,50]],[[80,-40],[-10,50]],[[60,30],[40,-40]],[[40,50],[-10,-10]],[[80,-20],[40,60]],[[10,-30],[-30,-20]]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
F1: flist[ix][1]; F2: flist[ix][2];
R: F1+F2; RR: R.R; tm: sqrt(RR);
tR: col(R); td1: col(F1-F2); td2: col(F2-F1);
/* diagnostics (b): added the sizes, size of F1 - F2, no root, sum of the parts */
g1: sqrt(F1.F1)+sqrt(F2.F2); g2: sqrt((F1-F2).(F1-F2)); g3: abs(R[1])+abs(R[2]);
rr: float(floor(100*tm+1/2)/100); md: dispdp(rr,2);
rw: tR+matrix([10],[0]); rwm: sqrt((R[1]+10)^2+R[2]^2);
badm: matrix([q],[1]);
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
